# Ford Zodiac Mk II four-door saloon, 1956-1962.
#
# The luxury member of the 1956 'Three Graces' range: the Zephyr shell with
# the larger six, the gold rear-wing script, two-tone paint and chrome wheel
# embellishers.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Zodiac
#
# Dimensions 4.534 x 1.702 m, wheelbase 2.718 m. Height was not established.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side elevation exists. Image 1 is a front
# three-quarter about 40 degrees off square; the flank is estimated from it
# and the other views within the published dimensions. The limitation is
# recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d) for a model-specific list, grade (c) for the later
# 1959-62 palette. Savoy Black, Ermine White, Ambassador Blue and Monaco Red.
# Two-tone was standard on the real car; the model carries single body
# colours and records that the contrasting roof is not represented. Weights
# 10, 9, 8, 8, total 35, provisional.
#
# Speed 145 km/h. Comfort 60/270, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 60. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1956 intro, retires staggered 1978-1981.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-zodiac-mk2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-zodiac-mk2.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-zodiac-mk2/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side elevation. The rear ribs are too
# restrained, and the bumper wrap and exact two-tone sweep are not reproduced.
# The model height of 1.50 m is an estimate. At 128 px the Zodiac grille, lamps
# and two-tone trim read as a Zodiac Mk II.


obj=citycar
